    {
      "id": "S17",
      "opening": "docker pull fails for me on rootless Docker",
      "has_gold": true,
      "oos": false,
      "kb_gap": false,
      "outcome": "resolved",
      "escalation_reason": null,
      "questions": 1,
      "fixes_sent": [
        {
          "tier": "kb",
          "cited": [
            "E1"
          ],
          "gold": true,
          "message": "The docker pull failure on rootless Docker is caused by an insufficient number of available entries in /etc/subuid or /etc/subgid.\n\n1. Check and ensure that sufficient entries (65,536 entries are recommended for most images) are provided in /etc/subuid or /etc/subgid. [E1]\n\nTo confirm: Confirm that running `docker pull` succeeds without throwing layer registration or lchown invalid argument errors.\n\nSources: E1 https://github.com/docker/docs/blob/main/content/manuals/engine/security/rootless/troubleshoot.md\n\nDid this resolve the issue?",
          "sources": [
            "`docker pull` errors"
          ],
          "evidence": [
            {
              "evidence_id": "E1",
              "tier": "kb",
              "url": "https://github.com/docker/docs/blob/main/content/manuals/engine/security/rootless/troubleshoot.md",
              "text": "**docker: failed to register layer: Error processing tar file(exit status 1): lchown <FILE>: invalid argument**\n\nThis error occurs when the number of available entries in `/etc/subuid` or\n`/etc/subgid` is not sufficient. The number of entries required vary across\nimages. However, 65,536 entries are sufficient for most images. See\n[Prerequisites](./_index.md#prerequisites).\n\n**docker: failed to register layer: ApplyLayer exit status 1 stdout:  stderr: lchown <FILE>: operation not permitted**\n\nThis error occurs mostly when `~/.local/share/docker` is located on NFS.\n\nA workaround is to specify non-NFS `data-root` directory in `~/.config/docker/daemon.json` as follows:\n```json\n{\"data-root\":\"/somewhere-out-of-nfs\"}\n```"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
